[standards/application/api/STD-APP-API-003-internal-external-api-guidelines.md#3342-backend-for-frontend-bff-pattern]

##### 3.3.4.2 Backend for Frontend (BFF) Pattern

Different backends optimized for specific consumer types:

```javascript
// Internal BFF - Full data access
app.get('/internal/api/v1/users/:userId', authenticateService, async (req, res) => {
    const user = await userService.getFullUserProfile(req.params.userId);
    res.json({
        ...user,
        internalId: user.internalId,
        auditTrail: user.auditTrail,
        systemMetadata: user.systemMetadata,
        sensitiveData: user.sensitiveData,
    });
});

// External BFF - Filtered data access
app.get(
    '/api/v1/users/:userId',
    authenticateCustomer,
    rateLimitCustomer(100, '15min'),
    async (req, res) => {
        // Ensure customer can only access their own data
        if (req.customer.id !== req.params.userId) {
            return res.status(403).json({ error: 'Access denied' });
        }

        const user = await userService.getFullUserProfile(req.params.userId);

        // Return filtered external view
        res.json({
            id: user.id,
            name: user.name,
            email: user.email,
            preferences: user.preferences,
            lastLogin: user.lastLogin,
            // Exclude internal fields, audit trails, sensitive data
        });
    }
);
```

